[[Simon Judeau|The Professor]] used Rippleburst on the rooftop of [[Dante Vale's house]] whilst attacking [[Lok Lambert]], but missed due to being blinded by Lok's [[Darkfog]]. Later, when the team were ambushed by [[Shauna]] and [[Wind]], she used Rippleburst on Lok, allowing [[Dervish]] to paralyze him and for her to steal [[Eathon Lambert's journal]] and the [[Amulet of Will]].{{source|The Secret of Two Generations}} 

The Professor again used this spell twice against [[Sophie Casterwill]]'s [[Sabriel]], when she was refusing to return to her amulet due to the effect of [[Dominator]]'s spikes. The first Rippleburst damaged the already injured Sabriel (due to the Professor's [[Poisonfang]]) while the second apparently took her out for good, her [[amulet]] being destroyed.{{source|The Mission}}

In the search for [[Nostradamus' Scrying Glass]], [[Hoffman]] used the spell in the [[Tower of Nostradamus]] to knock out [[Annette]]. He later used it in [[Nostradamus]]' hidden observatory at the same museum to defeat Sophie's [[Feyone]]. {{source|The Tower of Nostradamus}}

While the [[Huntik: Secrets & Seekers|Huntik]] team was trying to complete the [[Call of the Casterwill]] mission, 50 kilometers northeast of [[Mexico]] City, [[Kiel]] attacked [[Dante Vale]] using Rippleburst, but the latter countered it with [[Touchram]], resulting in a shockwave that knocked Kiel back. {{source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

[[Shauna]] cast Rippleburst on both hands (though without mentioning [[Doublespell]]) to target Sophie inside the [[Phoenix Volcano]], but Powerbonded Sabriel protected her [[Seekers|Seeker]] by getting in the way of the spell, going back to her amulet.{{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}}

This spell was used by [[Wilder]] against Sophie when the Huntik team were raiding [[the Professor's castle]], trying to complete [[The Professor's Dossier]] mission. She managed to dodge it.{{Source|An Ally from the Organization}}

